# High-blast-radius paths. A pull request that touches one requests the
# owner's review, and branch protection on main ("Block merge on official
# review requests") holds the merge until that review lands. The review gate
# sends at least these paths to the human lane (review/lanes.yml in
# bkennedy/infrastructure). A pull request that touches no path here, and
# no other path that the gate holds, can merge with no approval when its
# review is clean and its tests pass (INFRA-292).
#
# Each rule is a Go regular expression over the repo-relative path, followed
# by owners. Forgejo never requests a review from a pull request's own
# author, so this gates the pull requests of the agent accounts.
#
# Keep three lists in step: this file, the "High" list in AGENTS.md, and the
# rules for ghostty-font in review/lanes.yml. Each path here must also be a
# path that the gate holds. Change them together.
#
# test/ is not here on purpose. A rule here matches a path, not a change, so
# it would also hold each new test. The gate reads the diff: it holds a
# deleted test file, a skipped test, a removed assertion and an exit in a
# test file. A weaker assertion in place is for the review to find (the
# "Tests" paragraph in AGENTS.md).

# CI and the review kit. test.yml gives the required check on main, and the
# review workflow and its script come from the base branch, so a change here
# changes how each later pull request is tested and reviewed.
^\.forgejo/.*$                    @bkennedy
^scripts/forgejo-review\.mjs$     @bkennedy

# Agent instructions. AGENTS.md holds the review criteria.
^AGENTS\.md$                      @bkennedy
^CLAUDE\.md$                      @bkennedy
^\.claude/.*$                     @bkennedy
^\.agent/.*$                      @bkennedy

# What `bun install` puts on the machine: the bin entry, the files list, the
# dependencies and the lifecycle scripts. bunfig.toml and .npmrc do not exist
# today. Either one can point the install at another registry, so a pull
# request that adds one is a reviewed change. The rc rule below holds .npmrc.
^package\.json$                   @bkennedy
^bun\.lock$                       @bkennedy
^bunfig\.toml$                    @bkennedy

# All of the tool's code. It runs on the owner's Mac as the owner:
# bin/ghostty-font writes and restores the user's files and starts
# processes, and it imports from src/. The dotfiles pin bump that takes a
# new commit to the Mac shows a commit id, not the code. So the owner checks
# the code here.
^bin/.*$                          @bkennedy
^src/.*$                          @bkennedy

# Files that a tool finds by name and loads: a config file, an rc file, an
# env file. Also .gitattributes, which decides what a review diff can show,
# and editor settings, whose tasks run on the machine that opens them. The
# gate holds the same names in each repository.
^(.*/)?[^/]+\.config\.[^/]+$      @bkennedy
^(.*/)?\.[^/]+rc(\.[^/]+)?$       @bkennedy
^(.*/)?\.env[^/]*$                @bkennedy
^(.*/)?\.gitattributes$           @bkennedy
^(.*/)?\.(zed|vscode|idea|devcontainer)/.*$  @bkennedy
